# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Sheep Herder" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting out
0	section	Talking to Councillor Halgrive
1	line	Player	Hello. How are you?
1	line	Councillor Halgrive	I've been better.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What's wrong?
2	line	Player	What's wrong?
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	You may or may not be aware, but a plague has spread across West Ardougne. Now, so far, our efforts to contain it have been largely successful, for the most part.
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	However, some sheep recently escaped from a farm near the city. When they were found, we noticed that they were strangely discoloured, so we asked the mourners to examine them.
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	They believe that the sheep have become infected with the plague.
2	line	Player	Are you sure it's the plague?
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	Well the mourners seemed convinced and they're the experts. Even if it's not though, the sheep are clearly diseased in some way.
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	As the councillor responsible for public health and safety here in East Ardougne, I am in charge of dealing with this problem.
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	We need someone to herd these sheep into a safe enclosure, kill them quickly and cleanly and then dispose of the remains hygienically in a special incinerator.
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	Unfortunately, nobody wants to risk catching the plague, and I am unable to find someone willing to undertake this mission for me.
2	select	Start the Sheep Herder quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	I can do that for you.
3	line	Councillor Halgrive	You will? That is excellent news! Head to the enclosure we have set up on Farmer Brumty's land to the north of the city; the four infected sheep should still be somewhere in that vicinity.
3	line	Councillor Halgrive	Before you will be allowed to enter the enclosure, however, you must ensure you have some kind of protective clothing to prevent contagion.
3	line	Player	Where can I find some protective clothing then?
3	line	Councillor Halgrive	Doctor Orbon should have something suitable. You should be able to find him in the chapel just north of here.
3	line	Councillor Halgrive	Please also take this poisoned sheep feed; we believe poisoning the sheep will minimise the risk of airborne contamination, and is of course also more humane to the sheep.
3	box	The councillor gives you some poisoned sheep feed.
3	line	Player	How will I know which sheep are infected?
3	line	Councillor Halgrive	The poor creatures have developed strangely discoloured wool and flesh. You should have no trouble spotting them. There should be four in total.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	That's not a job for me.
3	line	Councillor Halgrive	I do not blame you adventurer. It is not particularly pleasant work. My problem remains however. If you know of anyone suitable please send them this way; time is of the essence.
3	action	end
1	option	That's life for you.
2	line	Player	That's life for you.
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	That's what concerns me... There might not be much life around here soon.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Councillor Halgrive again
1	line	Councillor Halgrive	Please... please find and dispose of those four diseased sheep as quickly as possible. Every second the risk of contamination grows! If you need some protective clothing, speak to Doctor Orbon in the chapel just north
1	line	Councillor Halgrive	of here.
1	cond	If the player lost the sheep feed:
2	line	Player	Some more sheep poison would be appreciated...
2	line	Councillor Halgrive	Certainly adventurer. Please hurry!
2	box	The councillor gives you some poisoned sheep feed.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player still has the sheep feed:
2	line	Player	I'll do my best sir.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Farmer Brunty
1	line	Player	Hello there. I've spoken to Councillor Halgrive. He has asked me to round up your sheep and slaughter them.
1	line	Farmer Brumty	Well, I always knew someone would have to. Make sure you're careful about it; there should be a cattleprod in the barn you can use to herd up the sheep.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Doctor Orbon
1	line	Player	Hello doctor. I need to acquire some protective clothing so that I can dispose of some diseased sheep.
1	line	Doctor Orbon	Protective clothing? I'm afraid I only have the one suit which I made myself to prevent infection from any contaminated patients I treat.
1	line	Doctor Orbon	I suppose I could sell you this one and make myself another, but it would cost you at least 100 gold so that I could afford a replacement.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Okay, I'll take it.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'll take it.
2	cond	If the player doesn't have 100 coins:
3	line	Player	Oops, sorry, I don't have enough money.
3	line	Doctor Orbon	That's okay. Just don't go near those sheep. When you can find the money come back here.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has 100 coins and 2 free inventory spaces:
3	box	You give Doctor Orbon 100 coins. He hands over a protective suit.
3	line	Doctor Orbon	These should protect you from infection.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has 100 coins but not 2 free inventory spaces:
3	line	Doctor Orbon	You don't seem to have enough room to hold the protective suit. Come back when you do.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player does not have the 100 coins:
3	line	Player	Oops, sorry, I don't have enough money.
3	line	Doctor Orbon	That's okay. Just don't go near those sheep. When you can find the money come back here.
1	option	Sorry doc, that's too much.
2	line	Player	Sorry doc, that's too much.
